  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Tuesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: An anticyclone aloft over the Desert\nSouthwest will slowly move westward into Southern California today\nthrough Sunday. The air quality is expected to be unhealthy for\nsensitive groups today due to smoke from area wildfires. An Air\nQuality Alert is in effect until 6 AM PDT Thursday morning. A few\nstrong thunderstorms are possible in Eastern Nevada this afternoon\ninto this evening. The primary thunderstorm hazards will be wind\ngusts near 45 mph and dangerous cloud to ground lightning \nstrikes. \n\nAs the aforementioned upper-level area of high pressure creeps\ncloser to the Silver State Friday through Sunday, the heat will \nbuild. Record heat is expected in Ely Friday afternoon. Near\nrecord heat is anticipated in Elko and Eureka Friday afternoon.\nRecord heat is expected in Ely Saturday afternoon. Near record\nheat is anticipated in Elko, Winnemucca, Eureka, and Tonopah\nSaturday afternoon. Record heat is expected in Ely Sunday\nafternoon. Near record heat is anticipated in Eureka and Tonopah\nSunday afternoon. Heat Advisories will likely be required for most\nof the forecast area Friday through Sunday. Here are probabilities\nof triple digit heat for select locations in Northern and Central\nNevada on Saturday, August 1st, 2026: \n\nBattle Mountain - 95%\nCarlin - 95%\nElko - 90%\nWinnemucca - 90%\nWest Wendover - 90%\nWells - 90%\nSpring Creek - 80%\nTonopah - 80%\nEly - 75%\nEureka - 75%\n\nHigh temperatures throughout Northern and Central Nevada Monday\nafternoon will be around five degrees above normal for this time\nof year. Maximum temperatures across the forecast area Tuesday\nafternoon will be seven to nine degrees above seasonal values.\nHeat Advisories may be required for parts of Northern and Central\nNevada Monday and Tuesday.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: Medium forecast confidence\nregarding smoke from area wildfires causing respiratory issues \nover Northern Nevada today. Medium forecast confidence in the\npossibility of a few strong thunderstorms in Eastern Nevada this \nafternoon into this evening. High forecast confidence regarding\nnear record heat in most of Northern and Central Nevada each\nafternoon Friday through Sunday. High forecast confidence in a\nmoderate risk of heat-related illnesses for heat-sensitive \ngroups each afternoon Friday through Sunday. No deviations from\nthe NBM model output.",
